### SpendSmart — auth requests for the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client).
### Click "Send Request" above each block. Cookies are kept between requests, so after
### verify-email / login the `me` request is signed in.
###
### Sign-up flow: register only writes to public.pending_signups. The account (users + profiles +
### 3 sources) is created by verify-email. To get the code without sending real email, start the
### server with SMTP off — in PowerShell (a single space; '' would just unset it):
###   $env:SMTP_HOST=' '; npm run dev -w server        (undo later: Remove-Item Env:SMTP_HOST)
### and copy it from the console:   [DEV] Verification code for you@example.com: 123456
### Then paste it into @code below.
###
### Check the database in Supabase → SQL editor:
###   select email, attempts, last_sent_at, code_expires_at from pending_signups;
###   select email, email_verified_at, created_at from users order by created_at desc;

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000
@email = test.user@example.com
@password = Correct-Horse-42
@code = 000000

### Password rules (client/src/lib/passwordRules.js = server/src/lib/passwordRules.js), checked on
### register and reset-password (never on login): 8–72 characters, an uppercase
### and a lowercase letter, a number, a symbol, no spaces at the start/end, not containing the
### email name or first name, not a common password. The confirmation must match.
###   400 { error: "<first problem>", code: "weak_password" }  |  400 { code: "password_mismatch" }

### 0a. Register with a WEAK password — 400 { error: "Add an uppercase letter (A–Z) to your password.", code: "weak_password" }
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "full_name": "Test User",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "correct-horse-42",
  "confirmPassword": "correct-horse-42"
}

### 0b. Register with a COMMON password — 400 { error: "That password is too common — …", code: "weak_password" }
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "full_name": "Test User",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "confirmPassword": "Password123!"
}

### 0c. Register with the email name in the password — 400 { error: "Don't use your name or email…", code: "weak_password" }
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "full_name": "Test User",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "Test.User#2026",
  "confirmPassword": "Test.User#2026"
}

### 0d. Register with a MISMATCHED confirmation — 400 { error: "Passwords don't match.", code: "password_mismatch" }
###     (confirmPassword missing → 400 { error: "Confirm your password.", code: "password_mismatch" })
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "full_name": "Test User",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "confirmPassword": "Correct-Horse-43"
}

### 1. Register (VALID: strong password + matching confirmation) — 201 { needsVerification: true, email, resendIn }; row in pending_signups, nothing in users
###    Again within 60 s → 429 { code: "resend_too_soon", secondsLeft }
###    SMTP failing → 502 { code: "email_send_failed" } and nothing is stored
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "full_name": "Test User",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "confirmPassword": "{{password}}"
}

### 2. Login BEFORE confirming — 403 { code: "email_not_verified", email, resendIn }
###    (also sends a fresh code if the last one is older than 60 s)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 3. Login BEFORE confirming with a wrong password — 401 { code: "invalid_credentials" }
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "definitely-wrong"
}

### 4. Resend code — 200 generic message, new code, attempts reset to 0;
###    429 { code: "resend_too_soon", secondsLeft } within 60 s of the last code
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/resend-code
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}"
}

### 5. Resend code for an unknown email — same generic answer (no account enumeration)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/resend-code
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody-{{$randomInt 1000 9999}}@example.com"
}

### 6. Verify with a WRONG code — 400 { code: "invalid_code", attemptsLeft }
###    After 5 wrong tries: { code: "too_many_attempts" } until a new code is requested (4.)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/verify-email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "code": "999999"
}

### 7. Verify with the code from the console/email — 200 { user }, sets the ss_session cookie.
###    The pending row is gone; users, profiles and 3 sources now exist.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/verify-email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "code": "{{code}}",
  "remember": true
}

### 8. Verify again (double click) — 409 { code: "already_verified" }
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/verify-email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "code": "{{code}}"
}

### 9. Me — 200 { user } when signed in, 401 otherwise
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

### 10. Logout — clears the cookie
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout

### 11. Me after logout — 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

### 12. Login with a WRONG password — 401 { code: "invalid_credentials" }
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "definitely-wrong"
}

### 13. Login (confirmed account) — 200 { user } and sets the cookie
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "remember": true
}

### 14. Register again with the confirmed email — 409 { code: "email_taken" }
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "full_name": "Someone Else",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "Another-Passw0rd!",
  "confirmPassword": "Another-Passw0rd!"
}

### 15. Validation error — 400 { error: "That email address doesn't look right.", code: "validation_error" }
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "full_name": "Bad Email",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "short"
}

### 16. Reset password from the emailed link (paste the token from the link / console) —
###     same rules: weak → 400 weak_password, mismatch → 400 password_mismatch, valid → 200 { user }
###     (a rejected password doesn't use up the link)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "PASTE-TOKEN-HERE",
  "password": "Fresh-Start-2026!",
  "confirmPassword": "Fresh-Start-2026!"
}
